# Real secrets live here (API keys, etc.) -- never commit this. The
# tracked template is .env.example, which stays all-blank on purpose.
# Found genuinely committed with blank values (no real secret leaked, since
# no commit ever contained a real key) but tracked at all was already the
# wrong pattern -- fixed by untracking it, not just adding this rule going
# forward.
.env

# Internal-only material: real-company recon, pre-sanitization originals,
# and anything else that must never leave this machine. Nothing in here is
# deleted, it's just excluded from what gets published/pushed. Lives under
# docs/ (not the repo root) so it sits next to the public docs it was
# derived from, but the ignore rule is what actually keeps it untracked.
/docs/internal/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/
# services/*/README.md's documented local-test setup (`python3 -m venv .venv`)
# creates this in-place -- never meant to be committed.
.venv/

# Wheels/model caches scripts/offline-up.sh downloads on the host and
# cleans up itself -- not meant to live in the repo even transiently.
_offline_wheels/
_offline_hf_cache/

# OS noise
.DS_Store
